     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and well above the 2,000 mg/day limit for extended-release. At that dose she'd be at serious risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCould this be a transcription slip? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**: 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg PO** at a different frequency.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note recording that it is above the labeled maximum. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
